        <mxCell id="invbox" value="Ordinal referencing invariants (BQGDMPR)&#xa;• three ordinal spaces — base (B and M rows), query (Q and G rows), predicate (P and R rows)&#xa;• row alignment within each space: M[i] describes b[i] · G[i] answers q[i] · R[j] lists the matches of P[j]&#xa;• value references across spaces: G cells and R cells are base ordinals ∈ [0, N)&#xa;• D (neighbor_distances.fvecs) is cell-for-cell aligned with G&#xa;• R records are variable-length (.ivvecs) — random access requires the IDXFOR__ offset sidecar&#xa;• R[j] = { i : M[i] ⊨ P[j] } — produced by compute evaluate-predicates; verified by SQLite re-evaluation&#xa;• downstream derivations: B+Q+R → F (prefiltered GT) · G+D+R → E (postfiltered GT)&#xa;(spec: 01-data-model.md §1.5 · prefilter-postfilter-facets.md)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="570" y="830" width="860" height="200" as="geometry" />
